    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23131" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γωνι-αῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on</i> or <i>at the angle,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Jb.</u>
					38.6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.372.19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στυλίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					3.22
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέρος τείχους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					5.3.5
				</span></i>
			; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γωνιήϊος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BCH</u>
					26.64
				</span></i>
			 (Delph.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>angular,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. ῥῆμα,</span> i. e. hard to pronounce,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				67
			</span></i>.</div>
